  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nThe central idea is to use a gradient-based optimization on a continuous relaxation of the step function, combined with multi-resolution refinement to escape local optima. Unlike the record holder approach that focuses heavily on continuous relaxation, this strategy emphasizes systematic grid refinement while maintaining the integral constraint. The key innovation is the explicit integration of multiple resolution levels (100, 400, and higher) with adaptive phase budgeting, ensuring sufficient time is dedicated to the most promising grids. This differs from previous strategies by addressing the potential grid-dependence issue through iterative upscaling and repair mechanisms, while also controlling the computational budget per resolution level.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\nThe optimization is formulated for a continuous function h(x) [0,1] on [0,2] with \u222bh dx = 1. The objective is to minimize:\n$$C_5 = \\max_k \\int_{0}^{2-k} h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx$$\nwhich is numerically approximated as:\n$$C_5 \\approx \\max_k \\left( \\frac{dx}{2} \\cdot \\text{cross-correlation}(h,1-h,k \\text{ to } -k) \\right)$$\nwhere dx=2/n_points. All computations use numpy's correlate in 'full' mode, then divide by dx.\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\na. Initialization:\n   - Sample initial_h_values down to 100 points using physical interpolation (x-domain [0,2])\n   - Set best_h to the initial solution\n   - Initialize n_current=100, target_sum=50.0\n\nb. Resolution progression:\n   - For each resolution level (100, 400, 800, 1600):\n        i. Interpolate from parent grid (if exists)\n        ii. Project to feasible [0,1] and integral=1\n        iii. Time budget = 30% of remaining time\n        iv. Apply paired coordinate descent with adaptive regularizations\n        v. Apply SLSQP final polish\n   - Promote best resolution to parent for next iteration\n\nc. Paired Coordinate Descent details:\n   - For i in 500-10000 sweeps per resolution level (except final polish)\n   - Compute correlation vector C for current grid\n   - Shuffle grid point pairs randomly\n   - For each pair, find minimal perturbation preserving integral constraint\n   - Update function values by gradient descent in 45-dimensional space (unrolled correlation)\n   - Project to [0,1] after each update\n   - Add random noise restarts (probability 0.05) with standard deviation controlled by grid size\n\nd. SLSQP Final Polish:\n   - Minimize penalty function: obj_lse(x) = max_correlation + (functions sum(x)-target)**2/2000\n   - Constraints: sum(x) = target; 0<=x_i<=1\n   - Initial point: current best solution\n   - Hyperparameter schedule: alphas = [10, 50] for n=400, [1000, 5000] for n=800\n\ne. Grid Transitions:\n   - Use physical (x-domain) interpolation with linear+projection fallback\n   - Repair function: \n        - Reallocation operator directly balancing integral\n        - Fallback if repair fails: greedy moves least significant entries\n\n4. Search Choices & Variations\n- Initial resolution: 100 points (physical grid)\n- Resolution progression: 400, 800, 1600\n- Budget allocation:\n    n=100: 400 seconds (31%)\n    n=400: 500 seconds (38%)\n    n=800: 400 seconds (31%)\n- Key hyperparameters:\n    - base_step_size = 0.01 * (2/n) \n    - adaptive_step_size by function value normalizing\n    - compression_factor = 0.98 for integral repair\n\n5. Compute Budget & Robustness\na. Dominant costs:\n    - Correlation computation: O(n^2) for large n (1600: 16e6 elements)\n    - Descent steps: 45 * (iterations) * (n) ~ 4500*n\n    - Repair: O(n) + O(n) projection\n\nb. Feasibility checks:\n    - After every major update: |\u222bh dx - target| < 1e-5\n    - Dynamic dimension: n = [100, 400, 800]\n    - Time monitoring: 20-second final repair margin\n    - Early termination: if C5 improvement < 1e-5 for 100 consecutive sweeps\n\nc. Fallback mechanism:\n    - Save best solution from each resolution\n    - Resume repair with: repair_solution(target_sum) until feasible or timeout\n    - If no solution: interpolate parent to current grid and optimize\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\na. Feasibility checks:\n    - 0 <= h_i <= 1 for all i\n    - |\u222bh dx - target| < 5e-5\n    - score = max_corr * dx (computed exactly as in evaluation)\n    - Tema   - ASCII \n\nb. Objective computation:\n    - Use np.correlate with mode='full'\n    - Post-process dx scaling\n    - Manual integral verification with Monte Carlo\n\nc. Final formatting:\n    - h_values: numpy array of floats [0,1]\n    - c5_bound: computed score (same as metric)\n    - n_points: final grid size\n\nd. Early termination conditions:\n    - Time < 200 seconds: return initial\n    - No improvement in minima discovered",
